Z||000000||Rodrv6||11-19-1999||02:52 PM||||I need some opinions.  A couple of years ago I had my '84 SE (four banger) off the road for about three months while I gave the car a total rebuild.  After getting it back on the road I had some problems with the engine running a fair chunk hotter than it used to. The gas mileage was (and is) down about 3-4 miles per gallon. I solved some of the warm running with a new radiator, but it is still warmer than it used to be.  The cooling system has been bled and has a new themostat and caps.  I am not losing any coolant and the thermostat has been checked against a thermometer. Also at my last emissions inspection the HC level at idle was too high. The engine is fairly fresh (about 40,000 miles since rebuild) and was in excellent tune.  Most of the fuel injection system sensors are less that two years old. Is it possible that sitting for that time may have caused the convertor to partially plug and cause these problems?  The convertor has ONLY 327,000 miles on it, so maybe I should quit being cheap and replace it?!?!?!<BR>Thanks,<BR>Rod||||reg||5
Z||000001||fierospeeder||11-19-1999||04:53 PM||||i know you can try a brake torque and i forgot what your really suppose to do, something that you should feel the car pushing hard foward and not slipping.  Dont do it too long, it can blow a gasket and heat up your trans.<BR>my book says to check it by<P>drive vehicle around 50 to 55<BR>lightly touch the brake pedal and check it for a slight bumpy sensation. TCC releasing.  A slight increase in rpm should also be noted.<BR>Release the brake and check for reapplication of the converter clutch and a slight decrease in engine rpm.<BR>if the tcc fiails to perform satisfactorily during the above test take your vehicle to the dealer for service(because this is a Haynes manual).<BR>Trans repair is expensive if you bring it in.  Got my Tbird turbo trans done rebuilt and after the rebuild some of my overdrive parts broke and had to bring it back.  Your saving about 300 if you bring the trans to the trans place.<BR>||||reg||1
